From 808594c13541f2b461c7afabe7d43fa43c76f380 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: Wallguard and Encrypted DNS services; ASUS DDNS removed;
 DoQ through DNS Director

rc/wallguard.c writes the feeds, safe-search and policy files, the cron jobs and
the wallguard-dir line into every dnsmasq instance (main and SDN), reconciles
the running dnsmasq with the switch directly (a notify_rc from inside the
service was dropped), fetches again at WAN up while lists are owed, and carries
the earlier test name's two settings and /jffs folder over once
(wallguard_migrate_legacy, after the /jffs permission sweep, lstat, no links
followed). rc/encdns.c starts rednsd with the certificate, opens 853 on the LAN
bridges, and for the block: REAPER_EDNS rejects 853 (TCP and UDP) and 443 to
the listed resolvers from br+, the provider names go NXDOMAIN, the router's own
DoT hosts excluded. Off by default, inert when off. init.c: a saved ASUS DDNS
(WWW.ASUS.COM*) is switched off once with a log line - asuscomm is not supported
on this firmware. dnsfilter.c: DNS Director's DoT block covers UDP 853 (QUIC).
firewall.c also carries the Port Trigger rule fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
